<p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Image Placeholder 1"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg" idx="2"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Notes Placeholder 2"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="3" sz="quarter"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:t>Marsh &amp; Roche, American Psychologist, 1997, p. 1187.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p/><a:p><a:r><a:t>The canonical statement of the problem. If the items being averaged are not a coherent</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>set, the average has no defined referent — you cannot say what the score measures. This</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>applies with more force to RMP than to formal instruments, because RMP imposes no item</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>structure at all.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p/><a:p><a:r><a:t>The three reviews shown alongside are the ones just walked through — physical appearance</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>at 3.0, vocal quality at 2.5, dancehall enthusiasm at 5.0. Marsh &amp; Roche were writing</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>about formal instruments with defined items. These are what the same critique looks like</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>with no items at all.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Slide Number Placeholder 3"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" idx="5" sz="quarter"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:notes>